# Supabase Configuration (REQUIRED)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here

# Application Configuration
VITE_APP_ENV=development
VITE_DEBUG_MODE=true
VITE_DEMO_MODE=false

# Optional: Analytics & Monitoring
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=your_sentry_dsn_here
VITE_PERFORMANCE_MONITORING=true

# Optional: Feature Flags
VITE_ENABLE_VOICE_FEATURES=true
VITE_ENABLE_IMAGE_GENERATION=true
VITE_ENABLE_VIDEO_GENERATION=true
VITE_ENABLE_SOCIAL_FEATURES=true

# API Keys (Server-side only - stored in Supabase secrets)
# These are managed through Supabase Edge Functions secrets
# DO NOT add these to client-side environment variables
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your_elevenlabs_api_key_here
# RUNWAY_API_KEY=your_runway_api_key_here
# RUNWAY_TOKEN=your_runway_token_here
# LUMA_API_KEY=your_luma_api_key_here

## Development Setup

1. Copy this file to `.env.local`
2. Fill in your actual API keys and configuration values
3. Restart your development server

## Security Notes

- Never commit actual API keys to version control
- Use Supabase secrets for server-side API keys
- Client-side environment variables are publicly accessible
- Use proper CORS configuration for API endpoints

## Production Deployment

For production deployments:
1. Set environment variables through your hosting platform
2. Ensure all secrets are properly configured in Supabase
3. Verify CORS settings for your domain
4. Enable security headers via CDN/server configuration

## GitHub Pages Deployment

For GitHub Pages deployment:
1. Set the following GitHub Secrets in your repository:
   - VITE_SUPABASE_URL
   - VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
2. Update the homepage URL in package.json
3. Configure your repository for GitHub Pages deployment